cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package, please cite the article below."
type: software
title: "DiscreteDynamicSurvivalAnalysis.jl"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/epirecipes/DiscreteDynamicSurvivalAnalysis.jl"
abstract: >-
  Bayesian inference for epidemic models from case line lists, in discrete time. Discrete
  dynamic survival analysis (DDSA) treats the infection and removal times of a line list as
  survival data whose distributions come from a deterministic discrete-time epidemic model, and
  samples the parameters with NUTS in Turing.jl.
keywords:
  - dynamic survival analysis
  - epidemic modelling
  - line lists
  - Bayesian inference
  - phase-type distributions
  - Julia
authors:
